# The clang-format BUILD `Check C++ style` judges this tree with (#1349).
#
# It is PyPI's clang-format at CLANG_FORMAT_VERSION in .github/workflows/build.yml --
# one release, one build, the same banner and the same output on Linux, macOS and
# Windows. The contour-workflows format-on-edit hook writes only with a binary whose
# `--version` line is listed here, character for character, and local-gate.sh refuses to
# `clang-format -i` with any other.
#
# Derived, never edited on its own: `ctest -R clang-format-version` refuses this file
# unless it declares exactly `clang-format version <CLANG_FORMAT_VERSION>`, so a version
# bump is one change to build.yml and this line together.
#
# To install that build, run `bash scripts/check-clang-format-version.sh --resolve`: when
# no clang-format on PATH is it, the refusal prints the install commands for this pin.
version: clang-format version 22.1.8
